  "id": "albanian_kreshnik_lahuta_epic",
  "name": "Këngë kreshnikësh (Albanian lahuta frontier-warrior epic)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Heroic epic of the Gheg-speaking highlands of northern Albania, Kosovo and the Rugova gorge, sung by a lahutar who accompanies himself on the lahuta, a single-string bowed lute of the gusle type. Its central cycle tells of the frontier warriors (kreshnikë), above all Muji and his brother Halili. Albanian-language epic singers were recorded for the Milman Parry Collection at Harvard before the Second World War, and the repertoire was later collected by the Albanian Institute of Folk Culture. The gusle card stands in for the lahuta.",
  "recipe": "classic modern këngë kreshnikësh, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. gusle. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
